  "about": "Candidate sources an admin can enable from the Admin page. None of these feed URLs could be checked from the build sandbox, so each starts as unverified: enabling one runs a test fetch first, and the Admin page shows whether it worked. No Twitter/X. Entries marked (buzz) measure how loudly a topic is talked about, not evidence (modules/review/sources.js); Medium tag feeds were checked on 2026-11-07, Reddit blocks automated readers. Sources that publish no feed (for example some lab news pages) aren't listed; add their posts with Submit a link, or use Find feed on their homepage. Kinds: journal means peer-reviewed venues (scored highest for evidence); people means a named researcher's or writer's own blog. 'findFeed' lists important sites without a known feed: the Admin page offers Find feed for each.",
